Wi-Fi (wmt_chrdev_wifi and wlan_drv_gen3, OPPO MT6765 wlan/) on Linux 5.10,
applied to the staged tree by tools/prepare-connectivity-sources.py
(patches.applied in connectivity-sources.json). wmt_chrdev_wifi needs no change.

- ACPI_STATE_D0 to D3 renamed WLAN_ACPI_STATE_*: they clash with acpi/actypes.h.
- procfs file_operations to proc_ops, struct timeval and do_gettimeofday to
  struct __kernel_old_timeval and kalGetTimeOfDay(), rtc_time_to_tm to
  rtc_time64_to_tm, struct timespec and get_monotonic_boottime to the 64-bit
  ones, init_timer to timer_setup, access_ok without VERIFY_*, ioremap_nocache
  to ioremap, (void) on getFwCfgItemNum for -Wstrict-prototypes.
- wakeup_source_init and _trash as wakeup_source_add and _remove.
- cfg80211 mgmt_frame_register to update_mgmt_frame_registrations, and the
  5.10 ndo_select_queue signature.
- File reads: set_fs and vfs_read/vfs_write to kernel_read/kernel_write, with
  MODULE_IMPORT_NS for the VFS namespace those and filp_open are in.
- kallsyms_lookup_name isn't exported: the MET trace lines use _THIS_IP_.
- CPU boost: kalBoostCpu() asks for each cluster's top speed through freq
  QoS. The EMI and VCORE OPP pm_qos requests are left out (no DVFSRC on 5.10).
- As stock (observed in the stock module): ARP_MONITER_ENABLE off, OPPO's
  /data/misc/firmware/active/ firmware path and its Algeria country group out
  (both under their OPPO guards), and a stray OPPO ucProcessed assignment gone.
- Every vendor command has .policy = VENDOR_CMD_RAW_DATA: 5.10
  wiphy_register() fails without one. NLA_PARSE and NLA_PARSE_NESTED use the
  _deprecated parsers, lenient as on 4.14.
- wlanRemove and exitWlan drop the CPU boost request, so no freq QoS request
  is left on a cpufreq policy after rmmod.
- Stock bugs: the RTS range check uses && and the last u4BWMapping arm is a
  plain else (values over 6 are already rejected).

